# A butcher's shop makes meat of the pigs the castle sends it: the butcher stands inside from the start, two pigs lie on the castle's flag (and the
# castle's stock holds nine more), a carrier takes them over the road to the shop's flag and on into the shop, the butcher works on each, and the
# meat goes back to the castle. The castle starts with 25 meat. The script fast-forwards to its second meat beyond that and takes a shot of the
# shop and its road. Run it on the layout, under either content set:
#   sh tools/play-run.sh butcher --layout layouts/butcher.jsonc --fps 10
#   sh tools/play-run.sh butcher --layout layouts/butcher.jsonc --fps 10 --content-set basic
wait 0.3
expect-at 13 10 building
expect meat = 25
fast-forward until meat >= 27 max 30000
scroll up 6 860 560
wait 0.3
dump meat-stored
shot meat-stored
expect meat >= 27
